  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 466.1,
   "w": 675.9,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "“The function of these correspondences is to underscore the depiction of the sanctuary as a world, that is,"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 486.5,
   "w": 675.9,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "an ordered, supportive, and obedient environment, and the depiction of the world as a sanctuary, that is, a"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 506.9,
   "w": 681.4,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "place in which the reign of God is visible and unchallenged, and his holiness is palpable, unthreatened, and"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 527.3,
   "w": 681.1,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "pervasive. ... The Temple was conceived as a microcosm, a miniature world. But it is equally the case that in"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 547.6,
   "w": 657.4,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Israel, the world, or I should say, the ideal world ... was conceived as a macro-temple, the palace of God"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 568.0,
   "w": 492.8,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "which is permeated with his presence and in which all is aligned with his will.”"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 603.9,
   "w": 635.6,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Levenson, Jon (1994). Creation and the Persistence of Evil: The Jewish Drama of Divine Omnipotence."
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 624.3,
   "w": 192.2,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Princeton University Press. 86."
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 660.0,
   "w": 672.7,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "“The Hebrew Bible is replete with descriptions of creation as a tabernacle which God has pitched (Ps. 104;"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 680.4,
   "w": 635.1,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Job 9:8; Isa. 40:22), or a house that God has established (with pillars, windows, and doors: Job 26:11;"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 700.8,
   "w": 679.1,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Gen. 7:11; Ps. 78:24). Consequently, the temple of Zion, as a sanctuary that God has established, becomes a"
  },
  {
   "x": 62.1,
   "y": 721.4,
   "w": 552.4,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "microcosmic metaphor for creation itself. This finds explicit expression in Psalm 78:69.”"
